                                        "sense_id": "c9285f1d-4fdf-3b80-b372-d2c16ac87f44",
                                        "entry_id": "96299868-b894-33dc-ba50-5fa52972bdeb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The cardinal number immediately following twenty-two and preceding twenty-four; 23."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2d52197-3707-4bb6-886e-68b90a6bd6e4",
                                                "sense_id": "c9285f1d-4fdf-3b80-b372-d2c16ac87f44",
                                                "text": "Reſolved, &c. That this Houſe doth accept of the Sum of One hundred Twenty-three Pounds of James Whitewick, of Coventry in the County of Warwick, Gentleman; his Delinguency being, That he went and reſided in the Gariſons held againſt the Parliament: Submitted before December 1645: His Eſtate, per Annum, Sixty Pounds; Perſonal Eſstate, Thirty Pounds: For which the Fine, at a Tenth, is One hundred Twenty-three Pounds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9b907d7-a38b-41cf-b698-f2ef8126dab8",
                                                "sense_id": "c9285f1d-4fdf-3b80-b372-d2c16ac87f44",
                                                "text": "Admiral Rooke, with twenty-three Men of War, having the Turky Fleet under his Convoy, was attacked off Cape St. Vincent by the whole French Fleet, under the Command of Admiral Tourville; twelve Engliſh and Dutch Men of War, and above four-ſcore Merchant-men, were taken or deſtroyed by the French."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93257eff-672f-401e-b408-ca626e958483",
                                                "sense_id": "c9285f1d-4fdf-3b80-b372-d2c16ac87f44",
                                                "text": "Maryland has exported nearly eight times as much as Connecticut; above six times as much as Rhode Island; twenty-three times as much as New Hampshire; almost eighty times as much as Vermont; and almost three times as much as the four minor states."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8542a8a5-9d0b-4dae-a4c6-6f30e3fcb848",
                                                "sense_id": "c9285f1d-4fdf-3b80-b372-d2c16ac87f44",
                                                "text": "Avignon was twenty-three kilometres away, on the second-class road N 570. We could be there in about half an hour. And we were, without stopping to admire any antiquities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbadc032-646a-4c07-a655-f3942c0ed078",
                                                "sense_id": "c9285f1d-4fdf-3b80-b372-d2c16ac87f44",
                                                "text": "Jehoahaz was twenty-three years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. His mother's name was Hamutal daughter of Jeremiah; she was from Libnah."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
